                      "title":  "Web safety capabilities",
                      "items":  [
                                    "Conversation analysis uses local rule modules and escalation logic.",
                                    "Privacy scanning combines browser-side OCR with phone, email, address and document exposure checks.",
                                    "Incident persistence is opt-in and stored in browser localStorage."
                                ]
                  },
                  {
                      "dot":  "rose",
                      "title":  "Android detection path",
                      "items":  [
                                    "Monitoring requires Android notification-listener access and the monitoring setting to be enabled.",
                                    "Only explicitly supported notification package names are processed.",
                                    "The current incident repository uses in-memory StateFlow and clears when the process state is lost."
                                ]
                  },
                  {
                      "dot":  "amber",
                      "title":  "Safety and trust limitations",
                      "items":  [
                                    "Pattern matches are indicators, not proof that abuse or fraud occurred.",
                                    "Users should review findings and choose appropriate safety actions.",
                                    "The web and Android paths are shown separately because no direct connection between them has been established."
